# Exercise 3 – Simple neural network (iris)

How this file is organised:
  - PART 1 - load the iris data
  - PART 2 - prepare the data (shuffle, split into training/testing, species -> [0, 1, 0])
  - PART 3 - create the network (random starting weights and biases)
  - PART 4 - forward pass   (Parts 2-6 of the explanation)
  - PART 5 - loss           (Part 7)
  - PART 6 - backward pass  (Parts 10-15)
  - PART 7 - update         (Part 16)
  - PART 8 - training loop  (epochs)
  - PART 9 - testing        (accuracy)
  - PART 10 - experiments: try different settings, save results.csv